  "page_type": "chart",
  "status": "active",
  "summary": "Factory ride (trim) height specs for 1970 coupe and convertible, standard and F41 suspension, with and without C60 air conditioning, as shipped and at curb weight. Gives front (Z, D at the control arms), sill-to-ground (J, K), wheel-centre (E, F) and fender-opening (P, R) heights in inches, so a restorer can check if the car sits at factory height.",
  "parts": [],
  "torques": [],
  "materials": [],
  "fastening": [],
  "notes": [
    "NOTE: Pull vehicle up 3 or more times & allow to settle, then measure dimensions. Measure \"J\" & \"K\" from under side of sill molding (appearance line) to ground.",
    "Z ± .25: centerline of lower control arm shaft front end to lowest point of steering knuckle, each dim. vertical to ground (front).",
    "D ± .25: rear, between centerlines at strut, dim. vertical to ground.",
    "J ± .50 OVERALL, ± .25 SIDE TO SIDE. J measured 30.50 behind front axle centerline; K measured 24.00 ahead of rear axle centerline.",
    "E and F: wheel centre ('0' line) heights front and rear; P and R: front and rear fender heights at axle centerline (as drawn).",
    "LOAD CONDITIONS: AS SHIPPED - oil, water, 2 gals. of fuel & recommended tire pressure. CURB WEIGHT - oil, water, full tank of fuel & recommended tire pressure (24 LBS front & rear).",
    "W-WITH, WO-WITHOUT, AVG-AVERAGE."
  ],
  "notes_internal": [
    "F41 column W/C60 is printed N/A in row Z with a vertical line down through all rows; filled down as N/A.",
    "Conditions: '354-390 LS5' printed as such (likely 454-390), copied exactly. 'M40A-ALL W/LJ1-LS5' printed LJ1, copied exactly.",
    "E/F/P/R meaning described from the side-view sketch; P and R arrows run from ground to the fender lip line at the axle.",
    "Revision record has only sym 2 (no sym 1 row). Rev AUTH 25949, DR FJM.",
    "Title block drawing number 3965172; DR DP/C1, CK ?-18-69 C1 (first digit faint), PREL 3-20-69, C/O A13; model 19000. Sideways 'K13' mark at lower left."
  ],
